# Findings the Trivy scans in CI should not report, one ID per line, each with the reason.
# The gate only fails on HIGH and CRITICAL; these are recorded so a full report stays clean
# and each one is a decision, not an oversight.

# Fixed UID and GID. OpenShift's restricted-v2 SCC assigns the UID from the namespace's range
# and rejects a pod that asks for another, so the chart sets runAsNonRoot and leaves the IDs
# to the platform.
AVD-KSV-0020
AVD-KSV-0021

# "Workloads in the default namespace": Trivy renders the chart without a namespace. The chart
# is installed into its own (see the README).
AVD-KSV-0110

# Trusted registries: which registries a cluster accepts is the cluster's policy
# (image.repository is a value), not the chart's.
AVD-KSV-0125

# Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK: Kubernetes ignores it; the chart has readiness and liveness probes.
AVD-DS-0026
